<title>FINLAND: HANDELSBANKEN CUTS ITS FINNISH PRIME RATE.</title>
<headline>HANDELSBANKEN CUTS ITS FINNISH PRIME RATE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Handelsbanken said in a statement on Monday it would cut its Finnish prime reference rate to 3.50 percent from 3.75 percent effective on February 17.</p>
<p>&quot;Inflation has remained low and inflation prospects are favourable. The money markets have been stable and the difference in long-term interest rates over Europe has narrowed further,&quot; Handelsbanken said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
